\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Rule audit of the three nets that pass gates A1 and A2, as discovered. Rule 3: a visit without a stop is in the language (shortest witness \texttt  {Gate In > Gate Out}). Rule 4: a reachable marking enables two stops at the same time. Rule 5: a mixed stop together with a separate delivery or receive at the same LL or HO2 area is in the language. Bound of rule 6: loops permit any number of stops; the stop guard enforces the planned number in the simulator. A3: rules 3 to 5 hold. Prec.: ETConformance (training).}}{78}{table.caption.47}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rq1_e2_audit}{{6.2}{78}{Rule audit of the three nets that pass gates A1 and A2, as discovered. Rule 3: a visit without a stop is in the language (shortest witness \texttt {Gate In > Gate Out}). Rule 4: a reachable marking enables two stops at the same time. Rule 5: a mixed stop together with a separate delivery or receive at the same LL or HO2 area is in the language. Bound of rule 6: loops permit any number of stops; the stop guard enforces the planned number in the simulator. A3: rules 3 to 5 hold. Prec.: ETConformance (training)}{table.caption.47}{}}
